+   const layout = ` REVIEW FILES GO IN ONE PLACE: docs/reports/lanes/${date}/${lane}/ directly (no subfolders; a file in a subfolder (lens-plan/, lens-out/, stage2/) is never read), named plan-<lens>[-<list id>][-pN].txt, out-<lens>[-<list id>][-pN].txt, in-<same name> inputs beside them, plus the file TASK; the second (fix) round (r2; two output rounds at most, RR-0385) is filed beside them as out-<lens>[-<list id>]-rN.txt with its in-<same name>: the close check reads it for findings like any out- file (each finding needs a verdict) and the round-1 file stays; a name not starting plan- or out- (fix-*.txt) is never read. The compliance lens reviews the WHOLE change: make the diff with \`git -c core.quotepath=false diff ${DIFF_ARGS.join(' ')} $(git log ${baseFull} --first-parent --reverse --format=%H -S@lane-${lane} -- '${'backlog/tasks/' + path.basename(task.file)}' | head -1) HEAD -- ${filesText(task.body).split(',').map((s) => s.trim()).filter(Boolean).map((e) => (/[*?]/.test(e) ? `'${':(glob)'}${e}'` : `'${e}'`)).join(' ')} ${(ruleTable?.exempt ?? []).map((g) => `'${':(exclude,glob)'}${g}'`).join(' ')}\` (never trimmed to core files; the base is the task's launch commit on the board, the first commit that holds this lane's assignee on the task file, so a lane already folded into the board still shows its whole change; only the paths of the Files line are in it, and the exempt paths are left out); lens-input splits the rule list at its headings and, when the diff leaves no room for a list part, splits the DIFF at file boundaries into chunks (never by hand, never inside a file); each chunk goes against every list part; the files are -p1..-pN, chunk by chunk, each stamped chunk c of m with its path list; the code-review, error-paths, ux and security lenses whose prompt would pass the bound use the same tool with their own template and no --list (\`lens-input --context ${ctx} --material <diff file> --out <lane dir>/in-out-<lens> --template .claude/review-templates/lens-<lens>.md\`) and are filed out-<lens>-pN.txt with their in-<same name>; one file alone over the room is refused naming the file and its size: report that to the orchestrator at once. A lane build or fix task closes in TWO commits (Spec 137 Rule 3 as amended for lane build and fix tasks): the work (code, tests, task notes) lands first; the closing commit carries only the lane's records (its report directory, the review context directory, the task file with the status, the decision record). The close check recomputes the changed paths of the task range (minus the exempt paths) and refuses when the chunks together are not exactly that list, when a chunk is not what that git diff prints for its paths, or when a stamp was edited. Fresh context every review round (RR-0378 step 5, 08_agents.md:529). Before the lens inputs of each review round (the first output round and every fix round) run in the worktree \`node scripts/analysis/backlog-brief.mjs --task ${task.id} --lane ${lane} --stage ${stage} --root ${wt} --board ${board} > /dev/null\`, which writes the next docs/reports/reviews/${task.id}/context-rN.md from your task file and the decisions of the board as they are then; the file named in the commands above is the launch file, so use the highest-numbered context-rN.md instead in every --context of that round and commit it with the round.`;
