er list: out-compliance-mobile-90.txt, out-compliance-mobile-98.txt, out-compliance-mobile-99.txt, out-compliance-mobile-100.txt, out-compliance-mobile-96.txt, out-compliance-surface-136.txt, out-compliance-storage-doc16.txt, out-compliance-five-words.txt, out-compliance-plan-protocol.txt, out-compliance-inc-F.txt, out-compliance-ms-F.txt. The joined run (`lens-input --list rules --lists <the compliance list ids>`, one set out-compliance-rules[-pN].txt for all the compliance lists) is an accepted form that is not the default (RR-0374, measured: joined whole documents found 10 of 15 findings against the per-document form's 14 of 15); a stage holding both forms is refused. Engineering lens, once per engineering list: the same commands with `--out <lane dir>/in-out-engineering-L --template .claude/review-templates/lens-engineering.md` on lens-input and the review tool; files out-engineering-eng-front.txt, out-engineering-eng-shared.txt, out-engineering-eng-back.txt. Commit each lens input beside its output (in-<output name>, the file the review tool read) and a file TASK holding exactly task-1; never edit a lens output (the review tool writes its REVIEW header, the close check recomputes the hashes). The close of this task is refused without an out-compliance output per list (or the joined set), an out-<lens>.txt for every other output lens named above, and the grounder file below (scripts/hooks/check-lane-close.mjs). The plan was ruled once, at the plan: the lane runs no plan lens. REVIEW FILES GO IN ONE PLACE: docs/reports/lanes/2026-11-19/BL-T1/ directly (no subfolders; a file in a subfolder (lens-plan/, lens-out/, stage2/) is never read), named plan-<lens>[-<list id>][-pN].txt, out-<lens>[-<list id>][-pN].txt, in-<same name> inputs beside them, plus the file TASK; the second (fix) round (r2; two output rounds at most, RR-0385) is filed beside them as out-<lens>[-<list id>]-rN.txt with its in-<same name>: the close check reads it for findings like any out- file (each finding needs a verdict) and the round-1 file stays; a name not starting plan- or out- (fix-*.txt) is never read. The compliance lens reviews the WHOLE change: make the diff with `git -c core.quotepath=false diff --no-ext-diff --no-textconv --text --full-index --diff-algorithm=myers --indent-heuristic --inter-hunk-context=0 --no-color --no-renames --src-prefix=a/ --dst-prefix=b/ -U3 $(git log refs/heads/wf2/board --first-parent --reverse --format=%H -S@lane-BL-T1 -- 'backlog/tasks/task-1 - Launch-me.md' | head -1) HEAD -- 'mobile/src/app/x.tsx' 'src/app/api/parcels/search/route.ts' ':(exclude,glob)docs/reports/lanes/**' ':(exclude,glob)docs/reports/reviews/**' ':(exclude,glob)src/tests/fixtures/surfaces/*/*.mobile.json' ':(exclude,glob)src/tests/fixtures/surfaces/*/*.web.json' ':(exclude,glob)src/tests/fixtures/surfaces/*/*.admin.json' ':(exclude,glob)src/tests/fixtures/surfaces/*/*.pdf.json' ':(exclude,glob)src/tests/fixtures/report-page/*.mobile.json' ':(exclude,glob)src/tests/fixtures/report-page/*.web.json' ':(exclude,glob)src/tests/fixtures/report-page/*.admin.json' ':(exclude,glob)src/tests/fixtures/report-page/*.pdf.json' ':(exclude,glob)src/tests/fixtures/report-page/props/*.mobile.json'` (never trimmed to core files; the base is the task's launch commit on the board, the first commit that holds this lane's assignee on the task file, so a lane already folded into the board still shows its whole change; only the paths of the Files line are in it, and the exempt paths are left out); lens-input splits the rule list at its headings and, when the diff leaves no room for a list part, splits the DIFF at file boundaries into chunks (never by hand, never inside a file); each chunk goes against every list part; the files are -p1..-pN, chunk by chunk, each stamped chunk c of m with its path list; the code-review, error-paths, ux and security lenses whose prompt would pass the bound use the same tool with their own template and no --list (`lens-input --context docs/reports/reviews/task-1/context-r2.md --material <diff file> --out <lane dir>/in-out-<lens> --template .claude/review-templates/lens-<lens>.md`) and are filed out-<lens>-pN.txt with their in-<same name>; one file alone over the room is refused naming the file and its size: report that to the orchestrator at once. A lane build or fix task closes in TWO commits (Spec 137 Rule 3 as amended for lane build and fix tasks): the work (code, tests, task notes) lands first; the closing commit carries only the lane's records (its report directory, the review context directory, the task file with the status, the decision record). The close check recomputes the changed paths of the task range (minus the exempt paths) and refuses when the chunks together are not exactly that list, when a chunk is not what that git diff prints for its paths, or when a stamp was edited. Fresh context every review round (RR-0378 step 5, 08_agents.md:529). Before the lens inputs of each review round (the first output round and every fix round) run in the worktree `node scripts/analysis/backlog-brief.mjs --task task-1 --lane BL-T1 --stage 1 --root /var/folders/8l/mcyqkj6d1pd5nm0bry4bql100000gn/T/bl-lane-waUgOW/wt-t1 --board /var/folders/8l/mcyqkj6d1pd5nm0bry4bql100000gn/T/bl-proj-3G4JUk > /dev/null`, which writes the next docs/reports/reviews/task-1/context-rN.md from your task file and the decisions of the board as they are then; the file named in the commands above is the launch file, so use the highest-numbered context-rN.md instead in every --context of that round and commit it with the round. Run the lenses in parallel, one call each, outputs out-<lens>.txt in the lane report dir; then a separate grounder rules every finding in GROUNDER.md (below). Session rule (Spec 08 section 7 rule 4 and section 5.3; COMPLY.2): a separate grounder rules on every finding. You do not rule on your own findings: list each finding with its id (`node scripts/analysis/rule-lists.mjs findings --dir <lane report dir>`), copy out-*.txt and FINDINGS.md into docs/reports/lanes/<date>/<lane>/ and leave the task RUNNING with "grounder owed"; the orchestrator launches a grounder that is not you, who writes GROUNDER.md there: headers `Grounder: <name>` and `Lane: <lane>` (the grounder is not the lane and not any assignee of the task); a line `Ruled: <output file> sha256:<12 hex> findings:<n>` for EVERY out-*.txt (and every plan-*.txt when the plan evidence is not on the board; rule-lists.mjs findings prints them; an output edited after grounding is refused); one line `<finding id> CONFIRMED|REJECTED|CONFLICT <repo path>:<line> "<quote on that line>" [reason: needed for REJECTED and CONFLICT]` per finding (the quote is checked against the repo, a lane report may not be cited). A build or fix task needs GROUNDER.md even with zero findings. The commit that sets the task BUILT is refused without all of it. ROUNDS (RR-0385, Spec 08 dated note 2026-11-22): round 1 resolves CRITICAL, HIGH and MED findings; round 2 resolves CRITICAL and HIGH only, and a MED the grounder confirms in round 2 gets the outcome line `<id> ruling:RR-0385` (the grounder decides it, the lane does not rule); LOW and NIT are recorded (pile or wontfix, 30+ character reason), not fixed or folded; there is no third round: a CRITICAL or HIGH still open after round 2 is reported with STATUS: blocked, for the operator.

